 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWS Global Accelerator API (2018-08-08). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Standard and custom routing accelerators are global configuration metadata reported DEPLOYED with no IpSets, DnsName or DualStackDnsName: no anycast address is allocated and no traffic is accepted or routed. Accelerators must stay disabled, so Enabled must be false at creation and cannot become true; IpAddresses (bring your own IP) is refused. Listeners, endpoint groups, endpoints, accelerator attributes (flow logs), custom routing traffic rules and BYOIP address ranges are not implemented; CreateListener, CreateEndpointGroup, AddEndpoints, ProvisionByoipCidr and their other operations return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501, so no accelerator has a listener when it is deleted. Cross-account attachments store their principals and resources without sharing anything with another account or checking the named endpoints and CIDR ranges; UpdateCrossAccountAttachment can only rename an attachment and refuses AddPrincipals, RemovePrincipals, AddResources and RemoveResources.",
  "title": "AWS Global Accelerator (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2018-08-08"
 },
